Z||000000||PaUL||04-19-99||06:39 PM||||Hey Ogre,<br>Just curious, what is your opinion on removing the steering damper on 84-87 Fieros?<p>Ive had mine removed for over 10 years with no ill effects, in fact I would say it has improved the steering, requiring less effort and increasing steering feel. I believe the bump steer you so vehemently warned me about is a non issue, any 98lb weakling could cope with it. I know you wont agree with me but I just had to come up with a rebutal to your warning that bump steer can "rip the steering wheel" out of your hands. Or was it, "bumpsteer can be strong enough to rip your arms out"
Z||000001||theogre||04-19-99||07:10 PM||||Fiero bump steer problems have never been that bad...... I've never felt they were that bad at all. I was trying to answer your question as to what it is, and what causes it. <p>I have had the non joy of driving other vehicles with extreme bump steer problems. they could and would tear the wheel out of you hands. Beleive me,,, it felt like you were getting you arems torn off.<p>I have what looks like the original stabilizer on mine..... I can't imagine it's doing very much most of the time.<p>out of curiosity.... what steering wheel is on your car? I've got the 4 spoke one. it's bigger than the stock one by an inch or 2. and the rim is fatter, and padded. I don't notice a number of problems, like the lack of power steering and road vibration. On the other hand people with the smaller wheel seem to notice both problems more.
Z||000002||PaUL||04-19-99||07:34 PM||||Ogre, my orig steering wheel was the ugly 4 spoke. I hated this wheel so I replaced it with a cheap aftermarket Grant GT steering wheel. This wheel has a much smaller diameter than the original, dont know the exact dimensions
Z||000003||theogre||04-19-99||07:41 PM||||nope. it's not exactly pretty. but it sure takes allot of fatigue out when I'm driving 3 hours on the NJ Turn Pike. Those dang skinny ass wheels most cars have really make my hands cramp. If you still have it, and don't want it I could use a spare if it's grey. (Finding one with th horn paddles in tact is a pain.)
